.TH OMX-MODGUI-SYNC 1 "2026-10-28" "omx-panel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-modgui-sync \- give a MOD GUI to every LV2 plugin that ships none
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-modgui-sync
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ --no-scan ]
.br
.B omx-modgui-sync
.B --check
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each LV2 plugin on the LV2 search list with no MOD GUI anywhere, writes a bundle named omx-modgui-<name>.lv2 in MODGUI_DIR: modgui.ttl and modgui/ made by
.BR "omx-panel modgui"
from the plugin's descriptor, and a manifest.ttl, so lilv adds the GUI to the installed plugin. The plugin's own bundle is never touched.
MODGUI_DIR may be a folder that also holds plugins.
.PP
The descriptor is, in this order, the plugin's declaration in omx-contract
.RB ( "omx-panel descriptors --installed" ),
the newest one in DESCRIPTOR_DIRS (written by plugin-hostd and plugin-qualify), or, unless
.BR --no-scan ,
one made by
.BR "plugin-hostd-probe describe" .
.PP
A bundle newer than its descriptor is left as it is. A bundle without the marker file .omx-modgui-sync is never written or removed; one with it goes away when its plugin is uninstalled or ships a MOD GUI of its own.
.PP
A plugin that cannot get a GUI never fails the run. One whose descriptor has no visible control (omx-panel modgui exit status 3) is counted as having nothing to draw; any other refusal is named in the summary. The run fails only when it cannot start: omx-panel, python3 or python3-lilv missing, or the plugins unreadable.
.PP
CLAP plugins have no MOD GUI and get no bundle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
say what would be written or removed, and change nothing
.TP
.B --no-scan
do not run plugin-hostd-probe for a plugin with no descriptor
.TP
.B --check
change nothing and report: the LV2 search list and where it came from, whether MODGUI_DIR is on it, whether the LV2_PATH that the mod-host and mod-ui units run with holds MODGUI_DIR (MOD-UI shows the bundles only if it does), and the CLAP search list
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LV2_PATH
the LV2 search list. Unset, it is plugin-hostd's default, which plugin-hostd and plugin-qualify read too: /usr/lib64/lv2:/usr/lib/lv2:/usr/local/lib/lv2
.TP
.B MODGUI_DIR
the bundles (default /usr/local/lib/lv2 for root, ~/.lv2 for a user)
.TP
.B STATE_DIR
the scans and work files (default /var/lib/omx/modgui-sync; $XDG_DATA_HOME/omx/modgui-sync for a user other than root)
.TP
.B DESCRIPTOR_DIRS
the scanned descriptors, a colon list (default /var/lib/omx/descriptors)
.TP
.B CLAP_PATH
only for
.BR --check :
the CLAP search list is CLAP_PATH, then ~/.clap, then /usr/lib/clap
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/omx/modgui-sync.conf
KEY=value lines for the variables above, read by the unit
.TP
.I omx-modgui-sync.service
runs the sync once; installed but not enabled (systemctl enable omx-modgui-sync). Enabled, it runs at boot and each time plugin-qualify-sync starts, after that sync has finished.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the run finished, whatever it could not draw; or --check reported
.TP
.B 1
the run could not start
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx-panel (1)
